<title>USA: Delta sets nonstop Atlanta-Caracas service.</title>
<headline>Delta sets nonstop Atlanta-Caracas service.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Delta Air Lines Inc said on Friday it will begin nonstop service between Atlanta and Caracas on December 7, 1997, in an attempt to build on its recently inaugurated Cincinnati-Atlanta to Brazil service.</p>
<p>Delta said in a news release that it also has filed an application with the Department of Transportation to begin service to Chile.</p>
<p>The company said it will fly 180-passenger Boeing 757s between Atlanta and Caracas, one flight each way each day. Southbound service was to begin December 7, with northbound service beginning the next day.</p>
</text>
